# Binaries and build output
/probavi
/dist/
*.exe

# `go build ./<dir>` writes the binary into the current directory, named
# after the package directory, and `go build .` from inside that directory
# writes it there. Both land in the work tree, and a 4.5 MB adapter binary
# reached version control this way once already, because the list below was
# kept by hand and one name was missing from it. It still is a list, but no
# longer only a list: TestEveryBuiltBinaryIsIgnored enumerates the main
# packages in the tree and fails when either place a build drops one is not
# covered here.

# go build ./internal/tools/<name>, and the same build from inside it
/adapterversion
/capabilities
/enginetable
/versionmatrix
/internal/tools/*/adapterversion
/internal/tools/*/capabilities
/internal/tools/*/enginetable
/internal/tools/*/versionmatrix

# The CLI, and the independent verifier. The verifier is its own module, so
# `go build ./cmd/...` for it runs from inside spec/evidence and drops the
# binary there; the repository root is out of its reach entirely.
/cmd/probavi/probavi
/spec/evidence/probavi-evidence-verify
/spec/evidence/cmd/probavi-evidence-verify/probavi-evidence-verify

# go build ./adapters/<name> drops the binary in the repo root
/postgres
/mysql
/mongodb
/mssql
/clickhouse
/mariadb
/etcd
/redis
/valkey
/sqlite
/duckdb
/prometheus
/cassandra
/opensearch
/influxdb
/victoriametrics
/elasticsearch
# …and `go build ./...` run from inside an adapter drops it beside the
# source, where the rules above do not reach
/adapters/*/postgres
/adapters/*/mysql
/adapters/*/mongodb
/adapters/*/mssql
/adapters/*/clickhouse
/adapters/*/mariadb
/adapters/*/etcd
/adapters/*/redis
/adapters/*/valkey
/adapters/*/sqlite
/adapters/*/duckdb
/adapters/*/prometheus
/adapters/*/cassandra
/adapters/*/opensearch
/adapters/*/influxdb
/adapters/*/victoriametrics
/adapters/*/elasticsearch
/oracle
/adapters/*/oracle
/neo4j
/adapters/*/neo4j
/solr
/adapters/*/solr
/firebird
/adapters/*/firebird
/h2
/adapters/*/h2
/couchdb
/adapters/*/couchdb
/qdrant
/adapters/*/qdrant
/weaviate
/adapters/*/weaviate
/aerospike
/adapters/*/aerospike
/questdb
/adapters/*/questdb
/tdengine
/adapters/*/tdengine

# Test and coverage artifacts
*.test
coverage.out
# The name ci.yml and spec/evidence's gate actually write.
cover.out

# Local evidence logs and keys (never commit!)
*.jsonl
*.key
*.pem

# …except the published conformance vectors, which are the point: a third
# party verifies them offline with the committed public key
# (evidence-schema.md §12). log_v0 and log_v1 were force-added before this
# rule existed, so a new one would have been dropped silently.
!/docs/schemas/evidence/examples/*.jsonl

# Editor/OS noise
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
